$$ (x+1)^2 + (x^2+1)^2 + \dots + (x^n+1)^^2 = \sum_{k=1^n} (x^k + 1)^2 $$
$$ = \sum_{k=1^n} (x^{2k} + 2x^k + 1) $$
$$ = \sum_{c=1^n} x^{2k} + 2 \sum_{c=1^n} x^c + \sum_c 1 $$
We have
$$ \sum_c x^{2k} = x^2 + x^4 + x^6 + \dots + x^{2n} = \sum_{c=1^n} x^{2k} = \sum_{c=1^n} (x^2)^k = \frac{x^{2(1+n)}}{x^2 - 1} = \frac{x^{2n+2}}{x^2 - 1} $$
$$ \sum_c x^c = x + x^2 + x^3 + \dots + x^n = \sum_{c=1^n} x^c = \sum_{c=1^^n} x^c = \frac{x^{n+1} - x}{x-1} $$
$$ \sum_c 1 = \sum_c 1 = n $$
Therefore,
$$ \sum_c (x^c + 1)^2 = \frac{x^{2n+2}}{x^2 - 1} + 2 \frac{x^{n+1} - x}{x-1} + n $$
$$ = \frac{x^{2n+2}}{x^2 - 1} + \frac{2(x^{n+1} - x)}{x-1} + n $$
$$ = \frac{x^{2n+2}}{x^2 - 1} + \frac{2x(x^0 - 1)}{x-1} + n $$
$$ = \frac{x^{2n+2}}{x^2 - 1} + \frac{2x(x-1)}{x-1} + n $$
$$ = \frac{x^{2n+2}}{x^2 - 1} + 2x + n $$

