We have
$$ \sum_c x^{2k} = x^2 + x^4 + x^6 + \dots + x^{2n} = \sum_{c=1^n} x^{2k} = \sum_{c=1^n} (x^2)^k = \frac{x^{2(1+n)}}{x^2 - 1} = \frac{x^{2n+2}}{x^2 - 1} $$
